skills/manuscript-prose-edit/references/llm-smells.md and prose-edit-contract.md adapt patterns, rules and
process steps from the following MIT-licensed projects. The text and examples here are rewritten for
scientific manuscripts; detector-evasion techniques from these projects are deliberately not included.

- humanizer, https://github.com/blader/humanizer
  Copyright (c) 2025 Siqi Chen. MIT License.
  Its pattern catalogue is based on Wikipedia's "Signs of AI writing" (WikiProject AI Cleanup).

- humanize, https://github.com/harshaneel/humanize
  Copyright (c) 2026 Harshaneel Gokhale. MIT License.
  Adapted: editing levers 3 to 8, the rhetorical-scaffolding checklist, the literal pre-output gate and the
  writer-profile step. Not adapted: perplexity injection, burstiness targets, RLHF-voice stripping,
  detector-scored selection and paraphrase passes.

skills/manuscript-integrity-check/references/kobak_2024_style_words.csv is recomputed from the yearly word
counts published by Kobak et al. (Science Advances 11(27):eadt3813, 2025;
https://github.com/berenslab/llm-excess-vocab) using the paper's published formula.

Ideas, rules and diagnostic tests were also drawn, in paraphrase, from a survey (2026-10-15) of open-source
writing skills, among them: AIScientists-Dev/academic-humanizer, matsuikentaro1/humanizer_academic,
Aperivue/medsci-skills, uchicago-dsi/ai-sci-skills, stephenturner/skill-deslop, labarba/sciwrite (CC BY 4.0),
taehyeonglim/academic-humanizer, Kiterlin/anti-defensive-writing, WantongC/journal-adapt-writing-skill,
K-Dense-AI/scientific-agent-skills, Orchestra-Research/AI-Research-SKILLs, conorbronsdon/avoid-ai-writing,
hardikpandya/stop-slop, Nanako0129/sepia, Aboudjem/humanizer-skill, seyedehsanhadi/sloptrim (Apache-2.0),
mshumer/unslop and eric-tramel/slop-guard (MIT unless noted). No text was copied from sources without a
licence; their ideas are restated in our own words.

skills/manuscript-prose-edit/references/claim-ladders.md adapts the claim-strength ladder ("Claim-Strength
Contract") from Yila-AI/awesome-research-skills, https://github.com/Yila-AI/awesome-research-skills,
Apache License 2.0. The rungs and markers are rewritten for scientific manuscripts.

The skills added in October 2026 (manuscript-peer-review, manuscript-reviewer-response,
manuscript-reporting-check, and the claim-support, number, submission-package and claim-strength checks
in the existing skills) reimplement design ideas from the projects below. No code or text was copied;
every script is an independent implementation and every rule is restated in our own words.

- Boom5426/Nature-Paper-Skills (MIT; parts Apache-2.0): comment splitting that keeps the referees'
  numbering, a review ledger with a landed field, reply-block order and tone, structural coverage checks,
  claim-source verification with four outcomes, data-availability and statistics-reporting audits, and
  behavioural evaluations with hidden rubrics.
- pedrohcgs/claude-code-my-workflow, Spark-To-Paper-Skills/paperjury, poldrack/ai-peer-review,
  amirkiarafiei/open-scholar-peer, GeoGeekLab/nature-reviewer-skills and xf686/Meet-Reviewer-2 (MIT):
  quote-verified findings, adjudication before reporting, routing and triage of concerns, the
  claim-consequence gate, identifier-grounded literature claims and matched negative controls.
- wanshuiyin/Auto-claude-code-research-in-sleep and wanshuiyin/Anti-Autoresearch (MIT): a fresh reviewer
  per round, the rule that a new number or citation must exist in the replaced text, deterministic
  adjudication, GRIM/GRIMMER/statcheck-style checks and corrupt-a-fixture tests.
- amos689/paper-preflight (MIT): registry lookups that never read a refused request as "not found",
  preprint-since-published and withdrawn-preprint checks, and positive confirmation or abstention.
- poemswe/co-researcher (MIT): a retraction ladder that records which source was checked, and a quote
  gate for cited claims.
- Aperivue/medsci-skills and aipoch/medical-research-skills (MIT): per-checklist licence verification,
  staleness fields and item states including "unclear because material was not supplied".
- THUROI0787/absent-author (MIT): a number ledger, hidden-text checks in PDFs, the claim ceiling and the
  author's checkpoint.
- pachterlab/paperpush (BSD-2-Clause): hidden-text, sensitive-content and anonymity checks of submission
  files.
- xmutfyh/dsh-plugin-writing-guard, heise3/academic-deai, SNL-UCSB/paper-writing-skill,
  drpwchen/paper-review-and-digest, Orchestra-Research/AI-Research-SKILLs and
  AIScientists-Dev/academic-humanizer (MIT): clause-level claim ladders with scope, null-result and
  evidence-status locks, content locks, blind red-team passes with rule-ID provenance and a stop rule,
  inference-gap names, the claim-type to required-evidence table, and the preserve list.
- WenyuChiou/academic-writing-skills (MIT): selecting checks by study design rather than discipline,
  and an optional per-paper record kept beside the manuscript.

Ideas only, with no text used, come from Imbad0202/academic-research-skills (CC BY-NC 4.0: criteria
committed before reading, judging a revision before the response letter, five revision states,
regressions versus previously missed issues) and from projects without a licence
(TobiasLee/Rebuttal-Skill: decide-first revision planning; HeartWise-AI/ai-writing-skills: the
negative-space test).

Reporting-guideline items in skills/manuscript-reporting-check/references/guidelines.yaml are
paraphrases with the official item numbers. Each entry records its source and licence; checklists that
are non-commercial or not openly licensed (for example CARE) are not reproduced.

evals/fixtures/manuscript-reference-check/sources/ holds plain-text conversions of Duncan et al. 2019
(Nature Communications, doi:10.1038/s41467-019-11112-0), Cross et al. 2022 (Frontiers in Genetics,
doi:10.3389/fgene.2022.1000667) and Lambert et al. 2020 (medRxiv, doi:10.1101/2020.05.20.20108217), each
licensed CC BY 4.0, with attribution and the changes made recorded in each file's header.
evals/fixtures/manuscript-reference-check/recorded/ holds trimmed public metadata responses from Crossref,
Europe PMC, PubMed, arXiv, DataCite and medRxiv, recorded on 2026-10-15 for offline tests.

skills/manuscript-revision-marks keeps the revision-mark format (`<!-- @rev ID rounds=N by=name:date -->`)
and the clean-twin, blind-spot and heat-map design of the manuscript ledger in dna-seq/just-dna-lite,
https://github.com/dna-seq/just-dna-lite (same authors), reimplemented on the standard library with LaTeX
support and review-ledger ids.
